## Decision

The engineering Gate is **FAIL/BLOCKED**. The implementation contracts and
the exercised P6 interaction slice pass, but the locked Gate P6 contract is not
closed. In particular, a complete V01-V07 visual matrix is absent and the
required D3D12 native-picking case is unsupported on the tested adapter. The
missing/unsupported evidence is classified as blocked rather than inferred as
PASS. Metal and release policy remain explicitly outside this Windows Gate.

## Severity-ranked blockers

### P0 - Required visual matrix is not closed

The locked P6 Gate requires screenshot agreement between selection, highlight,
Inspector, and the viewport. The specification also requires the V01-V07
visual/runtime matrix; the independent root contains one UI/highlight window
capture, but no complete V01 Grid, V02 Gizmo, V03 Parent-space, V04 Depth/X-ray,
V05 Delta-edit, V06 Topology-swap, and V07 DPI/resize set with the required
state and pixel assertions. The candidate acceptance report itself records
`R23` and `F39` as `blocked` with the message that the all-requirement visual
matrix is not closed. This is sufficient to prevent a Gate PASS.

Evidence: `p6-90-acceptance-report.json` (109034 bytes, SHA-256
`ba244aa9af3b642f97824c5d811b5d9e444d5b738f6a79c858b464b1855d7349`), and the
locked Gate wording at `docs/gltf-scene-editor-parity-task.md:901` plus the
V01-V07 obligations at `:1079-1085` and `:1426`.

